            <em>Instructions:</em> Show all work for full credit. Box your final answers.
            Leave enough space to show your steps clearly.
        </p>
    </introduction>

    <!-- ========================================================
         PART 1: KEY CONCEPTS
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="ws-idea-1-linear-equations">
        <title>Linear Equations</title>
        <p>
            Linear equations are also known as equations of first degree. That is, variables have <em>no written exponents</em>.
        </p>
        <p>
            In General, this would exclude equations with variables in the denominators of fractions, since they would have an 
            exponent of <m>-1</m>. However, we will see some equations with variables in their denominators that are <em>equivalent to</em> 
            linear equations.
        </p>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="ws-idea-2-solving-equations">
        <title>Solving Equations</title>
        <p>
            To solve an equation means to find all possible solutions.
        </p>
        <p>
            Good News! When solving an equation you can do anything you want—as long as you do it twice. Once to the whole left side and 
            once to the whole right side.
        </p>

        <algorithm number="no">
            <p><em>Strategy for Solving Linear Equations:</em></p>
            <ol>
                <li><em>Distribute</em> to eliminate parentheses</li>
                <li><em>Combine</em> "Like Terms"</li>
                <li>Use <em>Addition/Subtraction</em> to "collect" variables on one side, constants on the other</li>
                <li>Use <em>Multiplication/Division</em> to isolate the variable</li>
            </ol>
        </algorithm>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="ws-clearing-fractions">
        <title>Clearing Fractions</title>
        <p>
            To clear fractions from an equation:
        </p>
        <algorithm number="no">
            <ol>
                <li><em>Find the Lowest Common Denominator</em> (LCD) of ALL the fractions.</li>
                <li><em>Multiply</em> every term (on BOTH sides) by the LCD</li>
                <li><em>Simplify</em> each term. There should be no fractions.</li>
                <li><em>Solve</em> the new equation using your algebra skills.</li>
            </ol>
        </algorithm>
    </subsection>

    <subsection xml:id="ws-variables-in-denominator">
        <title>Variables in the Denominator</title>
        <p>
            When variables appear in the denominator, we must identify <em>restricted values</em>.
            A restricted value makes any denominator equal to zero.
        </p>
        <p>
            <em>Steps:</em>
            <ul>
                <li>Find the LCD of all fractions.</li>
                <li>Identify any values that make the denominators zero (restricted values).</li>
                <li>Multiply by the LCD.</li>
                <li>Solve the resulting equation.</li>
                <li>Check that the solution is not a restricted value.</li>
            </ul>
        </p>
    </subsection>

    <!-- ========================================================
         PART 2: PRACTICE PROBLEMS
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="ws-practice-problems">
        <title>Practice Problems</title>

        <p><em>Show all work. Box your final answers.</em></p>

        <!-- Problem 1 -->
        <exercise workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p><em>Problem 1.</em> Solve: <me>4x - 5 = 2(2x - x)</me></p>
                <space />
                <p><em>Answer:</em> <fillin /></p>
            </statement>
        </exercise>

        <space />

        <!-- Problem 2 -->
        <exercise workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p><em>Problem 2.</em> Solve: <me>x - 4(x - 5) = 2 - (2 - x)</me></p>
                <space />
                <p><em>Answer:</em> <fillin /></p>
            </statement>
        </exercise>

        <space />

        <!-- Problem 3 -->
        <exercise workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p><em>Problem 3.</em> Solve: <me>\frac{2x}{3} - \frac{5x}{6} - 3 = \frac{x}{2} - 5</me></p>
                <space />
                <p><em>Answer:</em> <fillin /></p>
            </statement>
        </exercise>

        <space />

        <!-- Problem 4 -->
        <exercise workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p><em>Problem 4.</em> Solve: <me>\frac{9}{4} - \frac{1}{2x} = \frac{4}{x}</me></p>
                <p>LCD: <fillin /></p>
                <p>Restricted Values: <fillin /></p>
                <space />
                <p><em>Answer:</em> <fillin /></p>
            </statement>
        </exercise>

        <space />

        <!-- Problem 5 -->
        <exercise workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p><em>Problem 5.</em> Solve: <me>\frac{1}{x-1} + \frac{x+1}{x^2 + 2x - 3} = \frac{1}{x+3}</me></p>
                <p>LCD: <fillin /></p>
                <p>Restricted Values: <fillin /></p>
                <space />
                <p><em>Answer:</em> <fillin /></p>
            </statement>
        </exercise>

        <space />

        <!-- Problem 6 (Additional Challenge) -->
        <exercise workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p><em>Problem 6.</em> Solve: <me>\frac{3}{x+2} - \frac{1}{x-1} = \frac{5}{x^2 + x - 2}</me></p>
                <p>LCD: <fillin /></p>
                <p>Restricted Values: <fillin /></p>
                <space />
                <p><em>Answer:</em> <fillin /></p>
            </statement>
        </exercise>

    </subsection>

    <!-- ========================================================
         PART 3: ANSWER KEY
         ======================================================== -->

    <subsection xml:id="ws-answer-key">
        <title>Answer Key</title>
        <p><em>For instructor use only.</em></p>

        <p><em>Problem 1:</em> <m>x = 5</m></p>
        <p><em>Problem 2:</em> <m>x = 5</m></p>
        <p><em>Problem 3:</em> <m>x = 3</m></p>
        <p><em>Problem 4:</em> LCD = <m>4x</m>, Restricted Values: <m>x \neq 0</m>, <m>x = 2</m></p>
        <p><em>Problem 5:</em> LCD = <m>(x-1)(x+3)</m>, Restricted Values: <m>x \neq 1, -3</m>, <m>x = -5</m></p>
        <p><em>Problem 6:</em> LCD = <m>(x+2)(x-1)</m>, Restricted Values: <m>x \neq -2, 1</m>, <m>x = 3</m></p>
    </subsection>

</worksheet>